WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.493
This is EstateHub. A property marketplace with a Next.js front end and a Django back end.

00:00:07.893 --> 00:00:15.033
Buyers search on a live map. Every pin is a price, and every filter is saved in the link, so a search can be shared.

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:24.617
Or they just describe it. AI search turns one sentence into filters. It works with OpenAI, Anthropic or Gemini.

00:00:25.717 --> 00:00:31.790
They open a listing, book a tour in a slot the seller has free, and reserve the home by bank transfer.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:39.162
Sellers get their own portal. They add listings, handle tour requests, and see what each property has earned.

00:00:40.162 --> 00:00:42.587
Both portals come in light and in dark.

00:00:44.087 --> 00:00:52.934
Your team runs everything from the admin console. Approve listings in bulk, verify identities, confirm payments and send payouts.

00:00:54.134 --> 00:00:59.781
Change the name, the logo and the brand colours from settings. No code, and no rebuild.

00:01:00.681 --> 00:01:02.445
And all of it works on a phone.

00:01:04.345 --> 00:01:15.496
The Django back end is included, with security fixes until 2028. 182 API routes, real-time chat and Django's own admin.

00:01:16.396 --> 00:01:23.536
Seventy-three finished pages, built on Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind and Django.

00:01:24.636 --> 00:01:27.125
EstateHub. Start with it already built.
